WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.033
-I'm so happy
you're still with us.

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:05.868
-Yes. [ Laughs ]
-I mean, I can't believe

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:07.767
that you did this
this morning, right?

00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:09.133
-I can't believe
I did it either.

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:10.601
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:12.968
-I want to get into all of this.
I want to also

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:15.167
get into the tour.
And look at how fun

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:17.801
the album is.
-Yeah. Brand-new album.

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:19.267
Just came out a month ago.
It's called

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:21.434
"It's the End of the World
but It's a Beautiful Day."

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:23.834
And it's our --
It's kind of true.

00:00:23.834 --> 00:00:26.367
Especially in these crazy times.
-Yeah.

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:31.200
-And we just put a brand-new
single, called "Seasons."

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.934
We're putting it out now,
on Monday.

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:37.634
And we have
a huge announcement today.

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:40.501
And this is the reason I climbed
the Empire State Building,

00:00:40.501 --> 00:00:43.100
because Thirty Seconds to Mars,
after six years,

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.334
we're going back on the road.
We announced a world tour.

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:49.267
And -- Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:52.267
[ Chord plays ]
-It's amazing.

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:58.033
-What -- You could have just
come on our show and said that.

00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:00.300
-Yeah.
-You realize. Right?

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:03.000
I mean, you didn't have to...

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.234
-Oh, there it is.
Oh, wow.

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:07.133
-Yeah, you could just -- Here.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.868
-Yeah
-You could just hold this.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.534
I mean, these are all
practical buildings.

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:12.400
-The only problem is,
this is the Chrysler Building.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:13.501
-Oh, yeah. Sorry about that.
Yeah.

00:01:13.501 --> 00:01:15.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:18.200
[ Muttering ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:22.033
-Yeah, yeah.
Yeah, it's that one.

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:23.701
But the tower's
been knocked off.

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:25.901
-It's this one, right?
-Uh...

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:27.834
No, it's that one there.
-It's this.

00:01:27.834 --> 00:01:29.000
-Yeah, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.567
-No, no, no.
-That's 30 Rock.

00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:34.000
-No, no, it's -- it's missing.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.467
-We don't have
the Empire State Building?

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:37.067
-It's on the wall.

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:40.734
-Oh, there it is.
Oh, it's in the screen.

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:43.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:46.133
You can't...
[ Laughs ]

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:48.467
It's real, it's real. Sorry.
Wow!

00:01:48.467 --> 00:01:50.734
It's the biggest building
on our backdrop.

00:01:50.734 --> 00:01:54.367
Sorry. But anyways...
[ Laughs ]

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:57.000
-Both of us are like...
But...

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.634
[ Laughter ]
But, dude, can I just say --

00:01:59.634 --> 00:02:01.701
I mean, I can't believe
I'm never --

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:03.601
never, ever
gonna meet King Kong.

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:06.534
And so I get to meet
someone else

00:02:06.534 --> 00:02:08.200
who climbed
the Empire State Building.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:11.434
This is fascinating.
What goes through your mind?

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:13.267
How do you even start it up
and go like,

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:15.300
"Hey, I have a weird idea"?
Like, who do you call?

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.634
-You know,
it's a great question.

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:20.400
It's a really good question,
but ever since I was a kid,

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.067
I was fascinated with
the Empire State Building.

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:26.501
It, to me, was a symbol
of New York City,

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:28.367
and New York City
was a symbol of a place

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:30.400
that you go to make
your dreams come true.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.534
I love this city, and
I always wanted to live here.

00:02:33.534 --> 00:02:36.634
I always wanted to be an artist.
And you know, for me --

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:38.300
And I don't know
if it was King Kong

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.934
or if it was, like,
the Guinness World Record,

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:42.133
but there was something
about that building.

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:44.801
I even had, like, a little toy
when I was a kid --

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:47.200
a little metal replica.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.100
That would have been perfect
here.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:50.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:52.868
-We'll make a note --
next time you come here,

00:02:52.868 --> 00:02:55.167
we'll get
an Empire State Building.

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:56.400
Yeah.
-So, yeah, it was just --

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.801
It was just a dream of mine.
I loved the climb,

00:02:58.801 --> 00:03:02.100
and it just seemed like
one of those impossible things.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.634
And it was very impossible
when we started.

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:08.434
We got 10,000 nos
before we got a single maybe.

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:12.501
And even then, we just really
got the final word

00:03:12.501 --> 00:03:14.133
a couple of days ago.

00:03:14.133 --> 00:03:16.901
-Which part of the building
did you climb, exactly?

00:03:16.901 --> 00:03:20.534
Like, the red part?
-Yeah, a little below that.

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:23.467
But I'll tell you,
this is called the fin,

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:24.801
the red part.

00:03:24.801 --> 00:03:26.300
And that's
the most exciting part

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.834
because you really feel like
you're floating above the city.

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:32.767
It's incredible.
And I wish I had a little video,

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:35.234
but what I climbed
are basically little --

00:03:35.234 --> 00:03:38.434
I put my feet on bolts.
They're tiny, little bolt heads.

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:42.300
And then I put my my hands on
either side of the windowsills,

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.300
which are quite sharp.
You can see

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:47.167
my hands are pretty beat up
from the climb.

00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:49.601
-Oh, my gosh.
It's not meant for climbing.

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:51.200
-Yeah.
-No, it's not.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.601
They didn't build that
for for climbing.

00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:56.601
-Appreciate you watching me
while I climbed today.

00:03:56.601 --> 00:03:58.701
-No problem. Yeah.
I couldn't believe that.

00:03:58.701 --> 00:04:01.267
You have great eyesight.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:05.434
We actually have a video
of you doing the climb.

00:04:05.434 --> 00:04:07.000
Let's take a look at you
in action here.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.434
We don't have any audio.
We can talk over it.

00:04:08.434 --> 00:04:11.667
But this is this morning.
That's Jared.

00:04:11.667 --> 00:04:13.734
That is you, buddy.
-Yeah, that's me.

00:04:13.734 --> 00:04:15.601
-I mean, wow!
-Yeah, I saw somebody...

00:04:15.601 --> 00:04:18.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:21.501
I saw somebody online.

00:04:21.501 --> 00:04:23.601
A friend of mine sent me a note

00:04:23.601 --> 00:04:26.834
saying a guy was convinced
it's A.I., that it wasn't real.

00:04:26.834 --> 00:04:29.434
But it's actually
very, very real.

00:04:29.434 --> 00:04:32.300
-You have the scabs to prove it.
-The scabs to prove it, yeah.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:36.601
-Were you nervous at all?
-You know, I wasn't.

00:04:36.601 --> 00:04:38.901
I really was so excited
to do it.

00:04:38.901 --> 00:04:41.133
It was very cold.
We got up at 3:15

00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:42.634
in the morning,
which was fun.

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:48.534
And it was about 41 degrees.
And I mean, it just added to it.

00:04:48.534 --> 00:04:51.334
The wind was really intense
up there, too.

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:54.634
-Why did you choose
that time of day?

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:56.968
-Well, we wanted
to get the sunrise,

00:04:56.968 --> 00:04:58.801
and it was part
of the arrangement

00:04:58.801 --> 00:05:01.000
that we made
to do it at that time,

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:04.234
because there are no people
on the observation deck.

00:05:04.234 --> 00:05:06.634
-People normally climb
the Empire State Building

00:05:06.634 --> 00:05:08.634
later, lunch time.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:08.634 --> 00:05:11.367
-12:30 1:00, everyone's climbing
the Empire State Building.

00:05:11.367 --> 00:05:13.534
-I think what they meant was,
they didn't want me

00:05:13.534 --> 00:05:15.434
to fall on someone
and hurt them.

00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:18.067
[ Laughter ]
Which is very nice.

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:19.400
-I can't believe
that you did this, buddy.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:22.033
I'm seriously in awe of this
and in awe of you.

00:05:22.033 --> 00:05:24.234
-Well, we haven't toured
in six years,

00:05:24.234 --> 00:05:25.934
and I wanted to do
something special.

00:05:25.934 --> 00:05:29.000
And our concerts are
about spontaneity.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.434
They're aspirational
in some ways,

00:05:31.434 --> 00:05:33.767
and really about
just living dreams.

00:05:33.767 --> 00:05:36.534
And this, to me, it's been
a longtime dream of mine.

00:05:36.534 --> 00:05:38.067
-This is a world tour
you're doing?

00:05:38.067 --> 00:05:40.634
-Yeah, it's a world tour.
And you know,

00:05:40.634 --> 00:05:42.634
it's a long time coming.
You know, my brother and I

00:05:42.634 --> 00:05:44.267
are so excited
to get back out there.

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:46.367
Thirty Seconds to Mars
has been gone for a long time,

00:05:46.367 --> 00:05:48.400
and we're ready.
-Your brother --

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:51.400
But you also then sang a song
after you climbed.

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:52.767
-Yeah.
-First of all,

00:05:52.767 --> 00:05:54.067
here's you just
sitting on the ledge going,

00:05:54.067 --> 00:05:56.200
"Yeah, I did that."
-Yeah.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:59.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:01.367
-[ Chuckles ]
That's pretty --

00:06:01.367 --> 00:06:04.167
That's pretty cool.
And then I actually have a video

00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:07.200
of you and your brother singing
"Seasons," your new song,

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.901
at the top of
the Empire State Building

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:10.234
this morning.
Let's take a look

00:06:10.234 --> 00:06:11.667
at that cool moment.

00:06:11.667 --> 00:06:15.267
-♪ People, they come,
and people, they go ♪

00:06:15.267 --> 00:06:18.367
♪ When the leaves change
and the colors they show ♪

00:06:18.367 --> 00:06:21.200
♪ Can you hold on
through the seasons? ♪

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:23.667
♪ Through the seasons, oh ♪

00:06:23.667 --> 00:06:25.367
-Yeah, I mean, come on,
that's...

00:06:25.367 --> 00:06:27.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:27.133 --> 00:06:30.133
You took what the Beatles
did on "Abbey Road,"

00:06:30.133 --> 00:06:31.734
when they performed
on the rooftop,

00:06:31.734 --> 00:06:33.667
and you topped them
by like six stories.

00:06:33.667 --> 00:06:35.834
-It was just --
It was a beautiful thing.

00:06:35.834 --> 00:06:37.634
And it's funny, sometimes
when you do concerts

00:06:37.634 --> 00:06:39.133
or little shows like that,

00:06:39.133 --> 00:06:41.334
it can feel
a little stiff or stale

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:43.167
because there was no audience.

00:06:43.167 --> 00:06:46.400
But it felt really amazing
to be up there with my brother,

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:48.634
and it was
an incredible experience.

00:06:48.634 --> 00:06:49.868
It was cool.
-Did you feel like

00:06:49.868 --> 00:06:52.100
you were just looking
at a model of the city?

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:53.667
I mean, did it look
like New York City?

00:06:53.667 --> 00:06:54.901
-You know, it does.

00:06:54.901 --> 00:06:57.033
It's the New York
that we all know and love,

00:06:57.033 --> 00:06:59.501
and it's a beautiful thing
to wake up

00:06:59.501 --> 00:07:01.968
with that city like that,
to watch the sun rise,

00:07:01.968 --> 00:07:04.133
to see that that whole city.
On one side --

00:07:04.133 --> 00:07:08.367
You know, Empire has 360 views,
and on one side,

00:07:08.367 --> 00:07:10.501
you see Central Park
and all the way north,

00:07:10.501 --> 00:07:11.601
and the other side, you see

00:07:11.601 --> 00:07:13.167
all the way down
to One World Trade.

00:07:13.167 --> 00:07:14.801
And it's incredible.

00:07:14.801 --> 00:07:16.734
I mean, I wish you could come
and do it with me sometime.

00:07:16.734 --> 00:07:20.934
-No, I'm busy that day,
but I would love to do it.

00:07:20.934 --> 00:07:24.367
I'm so happy for you.
-I hope that you come to a show.

00:07:24.367 --> 00:07:27.133
We're going to play Barclays
in...

00:07:27.133 --> 00:07:29.000
-I'll definitely be there
in Brooklyn.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:31.200
I will be there, absolutely.
It's on the ground?

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.501
-Yeah.
-Absolutely.

00:07:32.501 --> 00:07:34.467
I will be there.
I love this guy.

00:07:34.467 --> 00:07:36.367
Jared Leto --
one in a million, buddy.

00:07:36.367 --> 00:07:38.300
-You're the best.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:40.968
Check out his new album
and his upcoming world tour.

00:07:40.968 --> 00:07:42.968
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:07:42.968 --> 00:07:44.300
Stick around, everybody.

